<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toronto</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as York, Upper Canada</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Toronto is the capital of the Canadian province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>'s largest city, on the north-west shore of Lake Ontario. Founded as York by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-graves-simcoe">John Graves Simcoe</a> in 1793, it became the capital of Upper Canada and was briefly occupied by American troops in 1813. Renamed Toronto in 1834, it was one of the rotating capitals of the Province of Canada and grew into a centre of industry, finance and culture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toronto.jpg" alt="Toronto" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dillan Payne · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Toronto_Skyline_from_Snake_Island,_September_11_2026_(01).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
